Here is the commit message:
AMBARI-15173 - Express Upgrade Stuck At Manual Prompt Due To
 HRC Status Calculation Cache Problem (part2) (jonathanhurley)

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by issues in calculating the HRC (Host Resource Controller) status, which led to the upgrade process getting stuck at a manual prompt. This was primarily due to improper handling of transactional locks, affecting how certain database actions were executed concurrently without correct locking, potentially causing contention and failure in processing requests correctly. The previous implementation in `TransactionalLockInterceptor` was inadequate, necessitating the integration of locking behavior into transactional methods to ensure proper synchronization.

Here is the patch:
 import org.apache.ambari.annotations.Experimental;
